munology will prepare you for a leadership role in academic, government, or industrial research. With careers in the U.S. and abroad for domestic and international health organizations, our graduates apply research outcomes and innovations to benefit communities around the world.\nProgram Home\nRequest Information\nApply\nDetails, Dates & Deadlines\nProgram Details\nClass Format\nIn-Person, Full Time\nProgram Location\nUMB Campus\nProgram Length\n4-6 years\nCost/Credit Hour\nStudent Financial Services\nCore Requirements\nOnline application\n$75 application fee\n3 letters of recommendation\nOfficial transcripts\n300\u2013500 word essay\nProof of English language proficiency\nCV or resume\nDates & Deadlines\nInternational Applicants: November 15\nAll Other Applicants: December 1\nMolecular Microbiology and Immunology\nAdmissions\nBess Tracey, MEd\nAcademic Services Specialist\nmicrobiology@som.umaryland.edu\nAcademics\nDr. Eileen Barry\nProgram Director\nMeet Your Faculty\nOur GPILS programs consist of faculty in the basic science and clinical departments of the School of Medicine, School of Dentistry, School of Nursing, and a wide array of internationally recognized organized research centers and institutes on campus including the Center for Vaccine Development, the Center for Vascular and Inflammatory Diseases, the Institute for Genome Science, the Maryland Psychiatric Research Center, and the Institute of Human Virology, in addition to collaborations with the other University of Maryland campuses.\nView Faculty Bios\nNext Steps\nYour path to success starts here\nRequest Information\nRegister for an Info Session\nApply\nPrograms\nDirections\nSupport\nContact Us\nUMB Careers\nMobile UMB\nUMB Shuttle\nThe ELM\nUniversity of Maryland School of Graduate Studies\n620 W. Lexington St.\nBaltimore, MD 21201\n(410) 706-3100\nTwitter\nYouTube\nInstagram\nFacebook\nUniversity of Maryland School of Graduate Studies. All Rights Reserved.\nPrivacy Policy\nDigital Accessibility", 